    "title": "UD women's soccer advances to first A-10 final since 2022, tops Fordham 1-0 in semis - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joey DeBerardino ,\n1 hours ago\nDAYTON, Ohio (WDTN) – For the first time since 2022 the Dayton women’s soccer team is headed to the Atlantic 10 Tournament Championship, after the No. 1-seed Flyers edged No. 6-seed Fordham in the semifinal match Wednesday night at Baujan Field.\nA foul drawn inside the penalty box by sophomore Lauryn Contini set up a penalty opportunity for Kyra Karfonta, who is now 3-for-3 on the season in PKs.\nKarfonta, who was just named A-10 Defensive Player of the Year, provided the game’s lone goal in the ninth minute of the first half.\nThe win improves the Flyers’ record to 15-3-2 on the season and punches their ticket to the A-10 Championship final on Sunday at noon. As the tournament’s No. 1 seed, UD will host the match at Baujan Field.\nThe shutout was a program-record 14th on the season for senior keeper Batoul Reda Dayton defense. The Dearborn, Mich. native saw nine total shots and two on-goal in the match.\nDayton held the advantage in shots overall (17 to 9) and shots on goal (5 to 2).\nThe Flyers now host the Atlantic 10 Championship final on Sunday, Nov. 8 at noon against No. 4 seed Rhode Island at Baujan Field.\nURI upset No. 2-seeded Saint Louis, 4-2, on the road to earn the championship berth.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.",
